# Deliberately narrow: no repo-wide `text=auto`, which would renormalize every
# file and bury a real diff under a few hundred line-ending-only changes.
#
# These entries exist because `core.autocrlf=true` on Windows rewrites checked-out
# files to CRLF, and `sh` fails on a CRLF shebang. The push gate is a shell hook:
# a hook that cannot execute is a hook that protects nothing.
*.sh text eol=lf
.husky/** text eol=lf
